    "procedure": [
      "Retrieve and cite literature with Anna; seal the anna-research-record/v1 and re-verify every excerpt against the index.",
      "Convene the R.A.I.N. offline panel over Anna's sources and archive the transcript.",
      "Pre-register this definition in the R.A.I.N. registry before any data is fetched.",
      "Fetch seconds 60-660 of each listed Fantasia record by HTTP byte range; hash every byte.",
      "Detect R peaks (5-20 Hz band-pass, 330 ms refractory); exclude records whose valid-RR fraction is below 0.95.",
      "Resample respiration (1 Hz low-pass) and instantaneous heart rate onto a 4 Hz grid; high-pass both at 0.05 Hz; z-score.",
      "Run DRR RootingAnalyzer (lagged correlation, lags 1-12 samples, 199 circular-shift surrogates, max-statistic correction) on each subject's [respiration, heart rate].",
      "Run the identical test on mismatched pairs (respiration of subject i, heart rate of subject i+1) and on 20 synthetic directed and 20 synthetic independent AR(1) pairs.",
      "Submit measurements as rain-experiment-submission/v1; R.A.I.N. evaluates the criteria."
    ],
    "question": "Can DRR's surrogate-tested lead-lag analysis detect the well-established coupling from respiration to heart rate in real resting recordings, while not detecting it between different people?",
    "rationale": "External real-data validation for DRR, whose only prior external test (QBO) was not supported. Respiratory sinus arrhythmia is established physiology, so this is a positive control on real recordings: a sound lead-lag method must find it in matched pairs and must not find it between mismatched subjects, whose breathing and heart rate share a ~0.25 Hz rhythm but no causal link. Literature context comes from Anna (arXiv) and the R.A.I.N. panel; criteria were fixed before any coupling statistic was computed on real data.",
    "runner": {
      "adapter": "rain-pipeline: Anna -> R.A.I.N. -> DRR (rain-experiment-submission/v1)",
      "kind": "external",
      "repository": "topherchris420/dynamic-resonance-rooting"
    },
